---
import LegalLayout from '../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { getBusiness } from '../../lib/content';

const business = await getBusiness();
const locale = 'en';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Cookie Policy — EazyFix"
  description="Which cookies and local storage eazyfix.gr uses, why, and how you can manage them."
  locale={locale}
  business={business}
>
  <h2>1. What cookies are</h2>
  <p>
    Cookies are small files stored on your device when you visit a website. Browser
    <strong>local storage</strong> works in a similar way. They are used for the proper operation of the
    website and, where stated, for essential features such as the shopping cart.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Cookies and local storage we use</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Name</th>
        <th>Type</th>
        <th>Purpose</th>
        <th>Duration</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><code>eazyfix_session</code></td>
        <td>Cookie — strictly necessary</td>
        <td>Authentication for the admin area (<code>/admin</code>). Not used for regular visitors.</td>
        <td>Up to 7 days</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>eazyfix_cart_v1</code></td>
        <td>localStorage — functional</td>
        <td>Stores your shopping cart in your browser, only if you use the shop.</td>
        <td>Until you delete it</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>3. Third-party services</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Bunny Fonts:</strong> fonts are served from EU infrastructure. No cookies are used for this purpose.</li>
    <li><strong>Stripe:</strong> if an online shop with payments is activated, the Stripe payment page may set its own cookies under Stripe’s privacy policy.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. What we do not use</h2>
  <p>
    We do not use analytics, advertising, social media tracking or profiling cookies. That is why no
    consent banner for non-essential cookies is shown.
  </p>

  <h2>5. How to manage them</h2>
  <p>
    You can delete or block cookies and local storage in your browser settings. If you block
    <code>eazyfix_session</code>, you will not be able to sign in to the admin area. Deleting
    <code>eazyfix_cart_v1</code> empties your cart.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If non-essential cookies (e.g. analytics) are added in the future, this policy will be updated and
    prior consent will be requested where required.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
